Chapter: PbkdfStoredGuard
  cites Foreword chapter Pbkdf

 Track D item 19, the Pbkdf leg. pbkdf-verify walked both hashes to the length
 of the STORED one, so a stored record is what decides how far the read goes.

 Guarded because something runs it (red's ruling, extended to this leg
 2026-08-16): crypto-vectors:81 and :84 call pbkdf-verify. Production does not
 today. apps/secrets reaches pbkdf-hash from VaultCrypto:77 but builds its
 parameters as literals and never rebuilds a PbkdfResult from a file, so the
 hostile record below is not reachable through the vault as it stands.

 The existing test hashes a record and verifies it in the same breath, so the
 only records pbkdf-verify had ever seen were ones it had just produced itself
 (L-GAP).

 Row 4 is why the guard is not only about the fault. Eight bytes of a real
 hash compared to eight bytes of a real rehash agree, so a stored record
 truncated to any prefix verified TRUE against the right password.

 Row 7 is the discriminator. A 16-byte tag is a legitimate parameter choice,
 so a guard that demanded 32 bytes would show up there and nowhere else.

Section: Helpers

  show-bool : Boolean -> Text
  show-bool (b) = if b then "True" else "False"

  row : Text, List Integer, PbkdfResult -> Text
  row (label) (password) (stored) =
    label & " verify=" & show-bool (pbkdf-verify password stored) & " stored-len=" & show (list-length (stored.pbr-hash))

Section: Parameters

 Eight blocks and one pass, not the 4096 and 3 of the defaults: this arm is
 about lengths and offsets, and the default parameters cost seconds per row.

  cheap : PbkdfParams = PbkdfParams { pb-time-cost = 1, pb-block-count = 8, pb-hash-length = 32 }

  short-tag : PbkdfParams = PbkdfParams { pb-time-cost = 1, pb-block-count = 8, pb-hash-length = 16 }

 A block count of zero leaves the block array empty, and the last block then
 sits at offset (0 - 1) * 32.

  zero-blocks : PbkdfParams = PbkdfParams { pb-time-cost = 1, pb-block-count = 0, pb-hash-length = 32 }

  negative-blocks : PbkdfParams = PbkdfParams { pb-time-cost = 1, pb-block-count = 0 - 1, pb-hash-length = 32 }

Section: Records

  pw : List Integer = [112, 97, 115, 115]

  wrong : List Integer = [119, 114, 111, 110, 103]

  salt : List Integer = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8]

  genuine : PbkdfResult = pbkdf-hash pw salt cheap

 Sixty-four bytes where the rehash gives thirty-two. Unguarded, the walk
 indexes the rehash at 32 and the guest dies.

  doubled : PbkdfResult = PbkdfResult {
    pbr-hash = (genuine.pbr-hash) & (genuine.pbr-hash),
    pbr-salt = salt,
    pbr-params = cheap
  }

  truncated : PbkdfResult = PbkdfResult {
    pbr-hash = pb-take (genuine.pbr-hash) 8 0 [],
    pbr-salt = salt,
    pbr-params = cheap
  }

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (row "1-right-password" pw genuine)
    print-line-uni (row "2-wrong-password" wrong genuine)
    print-line-uni (row "3-doubled-hash" pw doubled)
    print-line-uni (row "4-truncated-hash" pw truncated)
    print-line-uni (row "5-zero-blocks" pw (pbkdf-hash pw salt zero-blocks))
    print-line-uni (row "6-negative-blocks" pw (pbkdf-hash pw salt negative-blocks))
    print-line-uni (row "7-short-tag" pw (pbkdf-hash pw salt short-tag))
  end

